---
description: Preserve canonical architecture and prevent duplicate implementations
alwaysApply: true
---

Before implementing, locate the canonical owner, trace the complete call path,
inspect related routes/RPCs/jobs/events, search decisions and known failures,
identify tenant/authorization/transaction/idempotency boundaries, and compare
OpenAPI with runtime.

Do not create competing implementations, duplicate pricing or resolution
logic, bypass OPS, implement security only in UI, replace atomic operations
with sequential writes, silently change public contracts, introduce new
required tenant environment variables, or return raw database rows from public
APIs.
